    24  ## News
    25  
    26  * [05/2024] Sotopia was presented at ICLR 2024 as a spotlight ⭐!
    27  
    28  
    29  ## Introduction
    30  
    31  Sotopia is an open-ended social learning environment that allows agents to interact with each other and the environment. The environment is 
designed to be a platform for evaluating and faciliating social intelligence in language agents. The environment is designed to be open-ended, meaning that
the environment can be easily extended to include new environments and new agents. The environment is also designed to be scalable, meaning that the 
environment can be easily scaled to include a large number of agents and environments.
    32  
    33  
    34  
    35  ```bibtex
    36  @inproceedings{zhou2024sotopia,
    37    title = {SOTOPIA: Interactive Evaluation for Social Intelligence in Language Agents},
    38    author = {Zhou*, Xuhui and Zhu*, Hao and Mathur, Leena and Zhang, Ruohong and Qi, Zhengyang and Yu, Haofei and Morency, Louis-Philippe and Bisk, 
Yonatan and Fried, Daniel and Neubig, Graham and Sap, Maarten},
    39    journal = {ICLR},
    40    year = {2024},
    41    url = {https://openreview.net/forum?id=mM7VurbA4r},
    42  }
    43  ```
    44  
    45  ## Help
    46  See [documentation](https://docs.sotopia.world) for more details.
    47  
    48  ## Get started
    49  
    50  ### Install locally
    51  We recommend using a virtual environment, e.g. with anaconda3: `conda create -n sotopia python=3.11; conda activate sotopia; curl -sSL 
https://install.python-poetry.org | python3`.
    52  
    53  Then:
    54  `python -m pip install sotopia; sotopia install`
    55  
    56  This will setup the necessary environment variables and download the necessary data.
    57  
    58  > [!TIP]
    59  > Having trouble installing? Or don't want to install redis for now? We are working on a public redis server for you to use. Stay tuned!
    60  
    61  OpenAI key is required to run the code. Please set the environment variable `OPENAI_API_KEY` to your key. The recommend way is to add the key to 
the conda environment:
    62  ```bash
    63  conda env config vars set OPENAI_API_KEY=your_key
    64  ```
    65  
    66  ## Easy Sample Server
    67  You can view an episode demo with default parameters with the following:
    68  ```python
    69  import asyncio
    70  from sotopia.samplers import UniformSampler
    71  from sotopia.server import run_async_server
    72  
    73  asyncio.run(
    74      run_async_server(
    75          model_dict={
    76              "env": "gpt-4",
    77              "agent1": "gpt-4o-mini",
    78              "agent2": "gpt-4o-mini",
    79          },
    80          sampler=UniformSampler(),
    81      )
    82  )
    83  ```
    84  or run
    85  ```bash
    86  python examples/minimalist_demo.py
    87  ```
    88  


